# Modseqs come from one sequence for the whole database, so a change in
# one mailbox moves the numbers that the next change sees in another.
# Under the per-mailbox counters every number below would be 2.
#
# The obliterator leaves the sequence about to hand out 2, so the first
# append takes 2 and the second takes 3, in different mailboxes.
#
# What must not come back is an OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ] for a mailbox that
# did not change. Each mailbox still records its own next modseq, and
# only its own changes write it, so the watcher below stays silent
# while the other mailbox is written. Revision 43 moved the modseq
# per-mailbox to stop those insubstantial responses, and this keeps
# that.
depends empty-inbox
send 1
a create msother
receive 1
a OK done
protocol imap watcher
receive 1
* OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 AUTH=ANONYMOUS AUTH=CRAM-MD5 AUTH=DIGEST-MD5 AUTH=PLAIN AUTH=LOGIN COMPRESS=DEFLATE ENABLE ID SASL-IR STARTTLS] imapscript.test.oryx.com Archiveopteryx IMAP Server (security checking disabled)
send 2
w1 login script script
w2 examine inbox (condstore)
receive 10
w1 OK [CAPABILITY IMAP4rev1 ACL APPENDLIMIT=38400000 BINARY CHILDREN COMPRESS=DEFLATE CONDSTORE ENABLE ESEARCH I18NLEVEL=1 ID IDLE LIST-EXTENDED LITERAL+ MOVE MULTIAPPEND NAMESPACE OBJECTID QUOTA QRESYNC RIGHTS=ekntx SORT SORT=DISPLAY SPECIAL-USE STARTTLS THREAD=ORDEREDSUBJECT THREAD=REFS THREAD=REFERENCES UIDONLY UIDPLUS UNSELECT UTF8=ACCEPT WITHIN] done
* 0 EXISTS
* 0 RECENT
* OK [UIDNEXT 1] next uid
* OK [HIGHESTMODSEQ 1] next modseq - 1
* FLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen)
* OK [PERMANENTFLAGS (\Answered \Deleted \Draft \Flagged \Seen \*)] permanent flags
* OK [UIDVALIDITY 1] uid validity
* OK [MAILBOXID (f...)] stable mailbox ID
w2 OK [READ-ONLY] done
use main
send 8
b append msother () {162+}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
Subject: one of two mailboxes
Date: Thu, 20 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

body

receive 1
b OK [APPENDUID 1 1] done
# the watcher examines INBOX rather than selecting it, so that it
# does not take the \Recent claim away from main
use watcher
send 1
w3 noop
receive 1
w3 OK done
use main
send 8
c append inbox () {162+}
From: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
To: Arnt Gulbrandsen <arnt@example.com>
Subject: one of two mailboxes
Date: Thu, 20 May 2004 14:28:51 +0200

body

receive 3
* 1 EXISTS
* OK [UIDNEXT 2] next uid
c OK [APPENDUID 1 1] done
send 1
d fetch 1 (modseq)
receive 2
* 1 FETCH (MODSEQ (3))
d OK done
send 1
e status msother (highestmodseq)
receive 2
* STATUS msother (HIGHESTMODSEQ 2)
e OK done
send 1
f status inbox (highestmodseq)
receive 2
* STATUS INBOX (HIGHESTMODSEQ 3)
f OK done
# msother keeps its message: DELETE refuses a nonempty mailbox, and
# obliteration removes the mailbox anyway.
end
